WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.620
Dione is the fourth-largest moon of Saturn.

00:03.051 --> 00:20.707
With a mean diameter of 1,123 km and a density of about 1.48 g/cm3, Dione is composed of an icy mantle and crust overlying a silicate rocky core, with rock and water ice roughly equal in mass.

00:21.371 --> 00:31.557
Its trailing hemisphere is marked by large cliffs and scarps called chasmata; the trailing hemisphere is also significantly darker compared to the leading hemisphere.
